# Supabase project "metapeek" (ref yncuzxstzcnfhmfciwqz) — rate-limit counter store.
# Copy to .env for local dev; set the same two vars in Netlify:
#   Site configuration → Environment variables (all deploy contexts).
# Without these, rate limiting falls back to a per-instance in-memory store.
SUPABASE_URL=https://yncuzxstzcnfhmfciwqz.supabase.co
# Project Settings → API Keys → secret key (sb_secret_…). NEVER the
# publishable/anon key, and never commit the real value.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional: bearer token for the API routes. This key does NOT come from
# Supabase, Netlify, or any other service — there is nowhere to "get" it.
# You generate it yourself and MetaPeek simply compares incoming
# Authorization headers against it. Generate one on macOS/Linux with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# When set (here AND in Netlify env vars): every API route requires
# "Authorization: Bearer <key>" — requests without it get 401, including
# the public web UI's own fetches — and valid-key requests bypass rate
# limiting. In other words, setting it switches MetaPeek into private
# mode; it is an emergency shutoff, not a partner fast lane.
# Leave unset for the public keyless API.
# METAPEEK_API_KEY=
